+## Built (Quarry side, branch innh/lane-d, behind `QUARRY_EDGE__API_KEY_AGENT_RUNS`, default 0)
+- U1 principal and route fence. `auth.rs`: `Claims.key_id` / `acting_user_id` (serde default, legacy tokens unchanged), `is_api_key()`, `key_id()`, `key_owner_user_id()`, `is_person()`, `SCOPE_BROWSER_AGENT`; `validate_and_normalize_principal` arm `api_key` (sub must be `apikey:<key_id>`, key id 1 to 128 printable bytes, owner present, no `user_id`, no `service_id`; the actor becomes the sub; a `key_id` on a user or service token is refused as ambiguous); `zdr_floor` counts a key like a user. New `api_key.rs`: closed reason list, `route_allowed` (nine method+path entries), `fence_decision` (switch, then scope, then route), middleware `require_api_key_route_fence` layered beside `require_service_route_scope` on BOTH authenticated routers in `routes.rs`. `run_limits.rs`: `QUARRY_EDGE__API_KEY_AGENT_RUNS` (read per request like `human_browse_enabled`; an unreadable value stops boot) and `QUARRY_EDGE__MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS_PER_KEY` (default 2, minimum 1).
+- U2 start binding. `GrantValidation.key_id` (HTTP/JSON now; the gRPC mapping stays empty until the proto carries it: fail closed). New `agent_routes/api_key_runs.rs`: `check_start_request` (switch, scope, no resume, no profile, grant required in every environment, run budgets must be `on`), `bind_key_grant` (session or empty kind, allowlist or empty mode, no parent or resource, `key_id` and `owner_id` equal the token's, canonical non-empty hosts that REPLACE the body's, a budget that bounds something). `lifecycle.rs`: key branch ahead of the human and ordinary branches, run class Agent, grant budget applied whatever the claim switch says, `RunEntry.key_id`, `agent.run.started` / `agent.run.refused` logs with ids only. A key grant presented by anything that is not its key (owner session, other person, service) is refused. `grant_boot.rs`: switch on with the no-op validator refuses to boot (`ApiKeyRunsWithoutValidator`).
+- U3 per-step and per-key rules. `admission.rs`: `validate_run_grant` takes the run's key id (the grant must still carry it; a key grant never backs a non-key run; policy always compared for a key); a key run with no grant is refused per action; sensitive actions (dialog reply, upload, download) refused on the action's kind before the driver or the broker is asked, and gate 10 repeats the refusal; `tabs.rs` same grant check. `run_registry.rs`: `try_reserve_keyed` counts live plus pending runs per key (429 `per_key_run_cap`, scope `key`). `run_live.rs`: a key is always `Agent`, `AgentIdentityBasis::ApiKey` with `principal_id` `apikey:<key_id>` (new verified variant in `step_receipts.rs`). `web_policy_edge::principal`: a key is Autonomous (it would have been Human). `live.rs`: the events stream ends with `done: token_expired` at the token's `exp`. Run scoping needed no new code: every allowed handler already compares the run's `actor_id` with the caller's, and a key's actor is `apikey:<key_id>`.
+- U4 docs and matrix. `docs/openapi.yaml` (startAgentRun description, 403 and 429 text, step note), `docs/CONTRACTS.md` ("API-key agent runs": token, allow-list, grant fields, start rules, ZDR, audit), `docs/ERROR_REASONS.md` (13 reasons plus `per_key_run_cap`), `docs/RUNBOOKS.md` (enable order, boot refusal, kill switches, the gRPC `key_id` note, checks), ZDR matrix row `agent_run_api_key` (golden JSON, `.sha256` and `docs/ZDR_MATRIX.md` regenerated with `QUARRY_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1`, then rerun green without it).
