+# INNH-6: Crawl `sitemap` discovery and per-page `scrape_options`
+
+Status: BUILT IN TESTS, DARK (6a and 6b both done; committed locally on `innh/lane-c`, nothing pushed). Two flags, both default off and on no stack: `QUARRY_EDGE__CRAWL_SITEMAP` and `QUARRY_EDGE__CRAWL_SCRAPE_OPTIONS`. With a flag off the 400 `unsupported_option` is exactly what it was. No stack was started, no live flag touched, no container swapped; the Temporal replay of an old history and the side-by-side evidence run are not done (see "Not verified").
+Lane: C (crawl/change/parse). Plan home: E3.7 sitemap half, WS14/WS5 contract. Estimate: 11 d (6a sitemap first, then 6b scrape_options).
+The sections "What exists" and "The gap" below are the pre-build reading of quarryv2-next. Paths under `apps/Ingestion Plane/Quarry-v2`.
+
+## What exists
+REQUEST CONTRACT `crates/quarry-edge/src/crawl_request.rs`: FIELDS table lists `sitemap` (:56) and `scrape_options` (:61). Actual refusals: :437-445 (sitemap: anything but the string "skip" is 400 unsupported_option "sitemap seeding is not built yet (F-t2-041)"), :446-452 (ignore_query_parameters, out of scope), :453-459 (scrape_options: any value 400 unsupported_option "until WS5 slice 4"). ParsedCrawl (:176) has no field for either. Unit tests known_but_unbuilt_options_are_unsupported_in_both_modes (:683), sitemap_skip_is_accepted (:703). Handoff crawl_handoff (routes.rs:993) builds job params at routes.rs:1081-1094 via forward_job_signed; nothing about sitemap/scrape. openapi.yaml CrawlRequest (:6633) documents sitemap enum [skip] (:6701) and scrape_options "Reserved" (:6708); SDKs repeat it (sdks/typescript/src/models/CrawlRequest.ts:77-89).
+
+ORCHESTRATOR: CrawlJobInput (workflows.go ~88) has Seeds/MaxDepth/MaxPages/Scope/ScopeMode/Robots only; CrawlInputFromParams (workflows/inputs.go) reads params.seeds or params.url; CrawlJobWF (workflows.go:558) runs a slice frontier, crawlJobDurableFrontier (:771) enqueues each seed with one FrontierEnqueue activity per seed; children via enqueueChildrenBatch (workflows/crawl_scope.go:168 -> FrontierEnqueueBatch activity, 500 per call, activities/crawl_frontier.go). Single funnel for page calls: runPageWith (workflows.go:204) -> RunPageInput (activities.go:165) -> RunPage payload map built by hand (activities.go:229+).
+
+EDGE PAGE EXEC: internal_run_page (routes.rs:1567) takes InternalRunPage (:1338) and calls `runner.run(&run_id,&url,prev_fp)` (routes.rs:1746) with InlineRequest::default_for(zdr) (pipeline.rs:93-104), i.e. DEFAULT cleaning. The scrape route already has everything for options: ScrapeOptions::from_value + resolve (quarry-core/src/scrape.rs:461, :560), is_default()/cache_admissible() (:980-995), InlineRequest{clean: CleanOptions{only_main_content,include_tags,exclude_tags,remove_base64_images,extractor}} at routes.rs:758-770 and PageRunner::run_with_inline_request (pipeline.rs:574). internal_run_page parses none of it.
+
+SITEMAP PRIMITIVES (dark/partial): `quarry-transform/src/sitemap.rs` (parse, parse_body with gzip + 50 MiB decoded cap, decode_body, sitemap_urls_from_robots; commit 2aa157c17; docs/SITEMAP_PARSING.md says no route calls them), canonical_url.rs (E3.7.6, aa41358ed), `map_routes.rs` (POST /v1/map: reads /sitemap.xml + max 5 nested via fetch_text lossy UTF-8, so no gzip, no robots Sitemap: lines; host scope via merge_and_scope; robots allow-filter; web-policy gate; SSRF heur). Crawl scope/robots enforcement already runs per page in run_page (crawl_filter.rs CompiledScope, RobotsEnforcement, routes.rs:1650-1700). Control stores job params as free-form JSON (only max_pages_requested inspected, jobs_lifecycle.go:210), so extra keys need no control migration. Crawl and batch are refused under ZDR, so neither option has a ZDR path.
+
+## The gap
+Two independent builds; ship 6a then 6b.
+6a SITEMAP: accept sitemap = skip | include | only (Firecrawl vocabulary; absent = skip) and actually seed. The Go activity cannot fetch safely, so add an edge-internal HMAC-bound route (pattern of /v1/internal/run_page: runtime token + x-quarry-run-sig, org in body) `POST /v1/internal/crawl/sitemap {org_id, url, scope, robots, max_urls, zdr:false}` that: fetches robots.txt via the existing RobotsGate and reads `Sitemap:` lines through sitemap_urls_from_robots, falls back to /sitemap.xml, fetches sitemap BYTES through the guarded driver chain (new fetch_bytes; compressed-size cap, SSRF heur, web-policy gate_url), parses with parse_body, follows nested indexes bounded (<=5 children, depth <=2, as map does), requires every sitemap host inside the crawl scope hosts (reject cross-host Sitemap: lines), filters each loc through CompiledScope + robots allow, canonicalises/dedups with canonical_url, caps at max_pages, returns {urls[], discovered, nested_fetched, skipped{out_of_scope,robots,duplicate,cap}}. CrawlJobWF calls a new SitemapSeeds activity behind `workflow.GetVersion(ctx,"crawl-sitemap-seeds-v1")` when params.sitemap is include|only, then enqueues URLs with enqueueChildrenBatch at depth 0 (never one activity per URL: history growth) before the loop; `only` skips seed-link following, `include` unions. Must work in BOTH durable-frontier and in-memory-frontier paths (in-memory keeps the frontier in workflow state, so cap or force durable for large sitemaps). Counts surface in existing run_started/page event payloads (no new EventType per CONTRACTS).
+6b SCRAPE_OPTIONS: accept `scrape_options` restricted to the per-page extraction subset of ScrapeOptions: formats limited to markdown|html|rawHtml|links|metadata, only_main_content, include_tags, exclude_tags, remove_base64_images, extractor, timeout_ms; keep `actions`, `actions_on_error`, `screenshot`, `pdf`, `json/summary/...` as 400 unsupported_option on /v1/crawl. Validate at the handoff with ScrapeOptions::from_value/resolve (same FieldError paths prefixed `scrape_options.`), stamp the canonical resolved JSON into job params `scrape_options`, add ScrapeOptions to CrawlJobInput/CrawlInputFromParams and RunPageInput (omitempty so non-crawl bodies stay byte-identical; additive, no GetVersion needed since activity inputs are not replay-compared), extend InternalRunPage with `scrape` (raw JSON re-validated in the edge: defense in depth), and in internal_run_page call run_with_inline_request with CleanOptions from the resolved options. When options are non-default, SKIP the page-cache read and write (routes.rs ~1748: put_with_ttl keyed only by fingerprint would poison later default reads) using cache_admissible(). Note ingest=true pages then feed the CLEANED markdown into Data Plane; document it.
+Out of scope: ignore_query_parameters, per-job webhook, crawl results route (INNH-12), actions in crawl.
+
+## Files
+`crates/quarry-edge/src/crawl_request.rs` (ParsedCrawl + parse; replace the three refusals; update tests :683,:703); `routes.rs` (crawl_handoff params :1081-1094, InternalRunPage :1338, internal_run_page :1567-1760, new internal route near :105-125); NEW `crawl_sitemap.rs` + `crawl_policy.rs` (flag read); `map_routes.rs` (extract shared fetch_text, merge_and_scope, host_in_scope); `quarry-transform/src/sitemap.rs` (maybe the XML-entity fix noted in SITEMAP_PARSING.md) and canonical_url.rs; `quarry-core/src/scrape.rs` (a CrawlScrapeOptions subset/validator or `for_crawl()`) and `crawl_scope.rs` if sitemap is carried in CrawlContext; `services/quarry-orchestrator/internal/workflows/{workflows.go,inputs.go,crawl_scope.go}`, `internal/activities/{activities.go,crawl_frontier.go or new sitemap.go,crawl_types.go}` + tests; services/quarry-control (no code expected; confirm params pass-through); `docs/openapi.yaml` (CrawlRequest 6633-6712), `docs/openapi-internal.yaml`, `docs/CONTRACTS.md` (section 9.4 neighbours + new section), `docs/CRAWL_SCOPE_ROBOTS.md`, `docs/SITEMAP_PARSING.md`, `docs/RUNBOOKS.md`, `docs/ZDR_MATRIX.md`/`zdr_matrix.rs` (internal route row), `tests/web_policy_routes.rs` route_manifest (internal route = Gated), regenerated `sdks/typescript/src/models/CrawlRequest.ts` and other SDKs, `scripts/openapi-route-allowlist.json`.
+
+## Flag
+Proposed, all default OFF: `QUARRY_EDGE__CRAWL_SITEMAP=on` (allow sitemap include|only at the handoff and serve the internal discovery route; off = today's 400/501) and `QUARRY_EDGE__CRAWL_SCRAPE_OPTIONS=on` (accept scrape_options and honour `scrape` in run_page; off = 400 unsupported_option as today). Orchestrator needs no flag: keyed by job param plus GetVersion 'crawl-sitemap-seeds-v1'. Untouched: QUARRY_EDGE__CRAWL_REQUEST_VALIDATION, crawl scope switch (crawl_policy.rs CrawlScopeSwitch; sitemap seeding should require scope enforce, else observe-mode would seed out-of-scope pages), QUARRY_CRAWL_DEFAULT/HARD_MAX_PAGES. Do not touch the live flags: scrape_options in crawl deliberately excludes actions/capture so it never depends on them.
