+## Contract change
+POST /v1/crawl request (response envelope unchanged): `sitemap`: enum [skip, include, only], absent = skip; `scrape_options`: `{ formats?: string[] (markdown|html|rawHtml|links|metadata), only_main_content?: boolean, include_tags?: string[] (<=32 selectors, <=256 chars), exclude_tags?: string[], remove_base64_images?: boolean, extractor?: readability|clean_full|raw, timeout_ms?: 1000..55000 }` with camelCase aliases as on /v1/scrape; same conflicts_with_only_main_content rule. Errors keep the shape: 400 BAD_REQUEST details.fields[] {path, code, message}, paths like `scrape_options.include_tags[2]`, codes invalid_selector|out_of_range|unsupported_option. With flags OFF current behaviour stays exactly (sitemap != skip and any scrape_options -> 400 unsupported_option). `data.effective` (WS14.S3 echo) gains `sitemap` and `scrape_options`. Job params gain `sitemap` and `scrape_options`. Progress payloads gain `sitemap: {discovered, nested_fetched, seeded, skipped:{out_of_scope,robots_disallowed,duplicate,cap}}` inside existing run_started/run_completed (no new event type). Internal: `POST /v1/internal/crawl/sitemap` request {org_id,url,scope,robots,max_urls} -> {urls:string[],discovered,nested_fetched,skipped{...}}; `/v1/internal/run_page` request gains optional `scrape`, response unchanged (consider an `applied_options` echo, see risks). Stored html/markdown artifacts reflect cleaned content; refs unchanged.
