+# INNH-7: `max_age` on scrape: accept it and respect it
+
+Status: done in tests (behind QUARRY_EDGE__SCRAPE_MAX_AGE, default off; not run on a live stack)
+Lane: A (scrape/extract). Plan home: E3.8 (slice E3.8.4 "URL cache freshness plus ZDR matrix row", 5.0 d, W3 batch B8, W3-estimate.md:45; NOT built per W2-closeout.md:199). Estimate: 5 d.
+Section 'What exists' and 'The gap' below were written by reading quarryv2-next before the build and are kept as the plan record. Built and tested 2026-10-31 on innh/lane-a. Paths under `apps/Ingestion Plane/Quarry-v2`.
+
+## What exists (NOT ACCEPTED, and the existing cache cannot serve a "max age" read)
+REQUEST SIDE: `max_age` / `maxAge` is not a field of ScrapeRequest (`crates/quarry-edge/src/routes.rs:451-499`) nor in ScrapeOptions OPTION_KEYS (`crates/quarry-core/src/scrape.rs:418-429`, 10 entries) nor REQUEST_KEYS (`scrape_contract.rs:36-48`, 11 entries). Sent today it is an unknown key: lenient mode ignores it with `warnings[] unknown_field` + `effective_options.ignored_fields` + `Deprecation: true` (scrape_contract.rs:205-227, 261-288; routes.rs:592-601, 657-662); strict mode (QUARRY_EDGE__SCRAPE_REQUEST_VALIDATION=strict) returns 400 unknown_field.
+
+CACHE POLICY: `quarry_core::cache::CachePolicy` (cache.rs:5-33) = {mode, max_age_s: u32, vary_on, stale_while_revalidate_s}; `ScrapeRequest.cache: Option<CachePolicy>` (routes.rs:457). Only `mode` and `max_age_s` are read: `should_read`/`should_write` (routes.rs:58-70) and `effective_ttl` (72-77), where `max_age_s` is the TTL of the WRITE (`put_with_ttl`, routes.rs:814-822, default DEFAULT_TTL_SECS 3600 at edge cache.rs:22). `vary_on` and `stale_while_revalidate_s` are read nowhere. BUG: `CachePolicy.mode` has no `#[serde(default)]` (cache.rs:7), so `{"cache":{"max_age_s":60}}` fails deserialization -> 400 `invalid_request` (routes.rs:564-573) although openapi.yaml:6727-6740 documents default read_write.
+
+READ PATH: the page cache is read ONLY when the caller supplies `prev_fingerprint` (routes.rs:678-688): PageCache key `quarry:page:{org}:{fingerprint}` (edge cache.rs:40-46, org segment since WS4.K, proven by cache_policy.rs:417 `page_cache_is_not_readable_across_orgs`). A fingerprint is a hash of the raw body, so a caller can only hit the cache after already fetching the page; no URL -> result lookup. A hit returns `ScrapeResponse::from_output(cached)` with no inline text (routes.rs:681-686) and does not meter. `cache_state` hit|miss|bypass is in effective_options (scrape.rs:1037-1046, routes.rs:645-654, 839). Age computable from NormalizedOutput.fetched_at (output.rs:14).
+
+ADMISSION: cache read/write only for default options (`is_default` scrape.rs:980: no named formats, no tags, readability extractor, no captures/actions), static/non-browser plan, default web policy, non-ZDR (`quarry_core::zdr::guard(zdr, WriteKind::Cache)`, routes.rs:673-676). Any Firecrawl-style request naming `formats:["markdown"]` (as the Innhenting playground does) bypasses the cache entirely; `max_age` would be useless unless that changes.
+
+PRE-BUILT BUT UNUSED: `ResolvedScrapeOptions::canonical_options_key()` (scrape.rs:1000-1034) and `cache_admissible()` (993) were written for "a URL-keyed result cache: quarry:scrape:{org}:{blake3(url, key)}" and are used only by their own unit tests (1336-1361, 1479-1503, 1395, 1450); `fingerprint(url, vary, js)` at edge/cache.rs:123 is `#[allow(dead_code)]`. `quarry-transform/src/canonical_url.rs` (W3-B1-04, `canonicalize`, line 86) exists for URL normalisation.
+
+DOCS/PLAN: `docs/GAP.md:61` claims "maxAge cache control ... Equivalent" (false; plan line 3462 lists it as CLAIM-FALSE to correct). Existing Redis-gated cache tests: `crates/quarry-edge/tests/cache_policy.rs` (read_write second call 163, bypass 224, write_only 285, max_age_s=0 default ttl 350, cross-org 417, non-default options bypass 510, browser signals 603, honest prior_block 693, default options 788, ZDR 850). Monitors use /v1/internal/change, not this path.
+
+## The gap (build only this)
+1. Contract: root-level `max_age` (milliseconds, Firecrawl-compatible; alias `maxAge`) added to OPTION_KEYS (scrape.rs:418, 10 -> 11; the unit test pinning keys against a fully populated value must be updated) as `ScrapeOptions.max_age: Option<u64>`, validated 0..=2_592_000_000 (30 d) with FieldError `out_of_range`/`invalid_type`, resolved into `ResolvedScrapeOptions.max_age_ms`. Absent = exactly today's behaviour; `0` = never serve from cache but still write; `>0` = serve a stored result for the same org + canonical URL + options when `now - fetched_at <= max_age`.
+2. URL-keyed result cache (new, org-scoped): key `quarry:scrape:{org}:{blake3(canonical_url, canonical_options_key)}` -> JSON of NormalizedOutput (+ run metadata to rebuild the response), TTL = effective_ttl. Written on every cache-eligible success when `cache_allowed && should_write` (routes.rs:814 area), read when `max_age` is set (routes.rs:678 area) BEFORE the driver is built. Empty org id never a key (mirror PageCache::key). Do NOT key by fingerprint (two option sets over the same body would overwrite each other's artifact refs under `quarry:page:{org}:{fp}`).
+3. Admission widens to option-bearing requests: replace `cache_admissible` with "no capture, no actions, non-browser plan, default web policy, non-ZDR, no AI formats, no profile/credentials" with the OPTIONS KEY inside the cache key, so named formats / tags / extractor become cacheable per distinct key. (INNH-1's AI formats stay uncached in v1.)
+4. On a hit asking for inline formats (markdown/html/rawHtml), rebuild inline parts from stored artifacts (`output.formats.markdown/html/raw` ids via `state.artifacts.get`, artifact_store.rs:119) so no page text is stored in Redis; a missing/expired artifact = MISS and refetch. Hits return the ORIGINAL `fetched_at`.
+5. Response (additive): `effective_options.cache_state` exists; add `effective_options.cached_at` (RFC 3339) and `cache_age_ms` on a hit, plus warning `max_age_ignored_zdr` under ZDR (never read/write, no URL key stored even hashed, plan ADR topic 4). Hits are not metered as `scrape.page` (unchanged current hit-path behaviour routes.rs:681-686): record as an explicit decision.
