+
+Order: 1, 2, 9 first (the Innhenting UI reads 1 and 9 first), then 7, 4, 6, 11, 12, 5, 3, 8. Item 10: design note first (`INNH-10-design.md`), one Opus security review, then build behind a default-off flag. Item 13: assess only.
+Lanes (max 4 agents): A scrape/extract (1, 2, 3, 7); B control/orchestrator (9, 5, 12); C crawl/change/parse (4, 6, 11); D design for 10, and 8.
+
+Rules summary:
+- No live flag changes: QUARRY_EDGE__SCRAPE_ACTIONS, SCRAPE_CAPTURE, JOB_CONTROL, AI_FORMATS (with MODEL_PLANE_URL), QUARRY_SCHEDULE_CAPABILITIES. New behaviour ships behind a default-off flag or is additive.
+- Prove on a side-by-side stack or in tests; no rebuild or swap of live containers without asking.
+- The Innhenting session (local_505b1bcc) owns the gateway routes and SPA (`apps/Frontend Plane/verevonv3`). Quarry/control/orchestrator side plus `docs/openapi.yaml` and CONTRACTS.md are ours. Message it when items 1 and 9 land.
+- Local commits only on quarryv2-next with the Co-Authored-By trailer; no push, no PR, no `--no-verify`. Hot files routes.rs/main.rs/lib.rs/step_receipts.rs carry another session's uncommitted edits: commit own hunks from HEAD blobs.
+- Stop at 85% weekly usage or 80% of the 5 h window; stop if C: free space drops below 8 GB.
+
+Cross-cutting findings that change the brief:
+- `QUARRY_EDGE__AI_FORMATS` does NOT exist in code (only in a pending docs-contract test and plan prose). Nothing gates scrape AI formats or extract beyond `QUARRY_EDGE__MODEL_PLANE_URL`, and the model lane (`model-invoke`) is `granted:false` with the Model Plane refusing service principals on /v1/invoke. There is no production enablement path until WS16.S1-S3 and decision X-7 (items 1, 2, 3, 8).
+- Control webhooks have no org_id and fanoutWebhooks is global: a cross-tenant leak waiting on any tenant-facing route (items 5, 13b). Fix before exposing any webhook API.
+- pg `CreditUsage` SQL counts every event as 1 credit, so team credits are inflated versus per-job figures (item 9).
+- Shared edits to avoid double work: items 4 and 12 both add `markdown_artifact_id` to InternalRunPageResult / RunPageResult; items 5 and 13b are one webhook build; item 1's engine fixes serve item 2.
