+INNH-3 | review | The `error` field itself carries an operator variable name (`QUARRY_EDGE__MODEL_PLANE_URL is not set on this deployment`, case 1) and the status file tells the UI to show `error` as the reason, while also saying never to tell a person to set a variable. The UI will print an env name to end users. Only names are exposed (no value, URL, host or token; tests pin that), but the three texts also reveal deployment state to any authenticated non-ZDR caller (Model Plane configured or not, credential held or not) and the case-2 hint names "the auth dev bypass" and the planning ids WS16.S1 to S3 / X-7. Keep operator detail in `hint` only and make `error` user-safe ("structured extraction is not available on this deployment"), or return the same `error` for all three and tell them apart by `details.reason`.
+INNH-3 | review | The RUNBOOKS dev path says to leave `QUARRY_EDGE__QUARRY_SERVICE_API_KEY` unset so the dev token is used. The Ingestion compose declares it `${QUARRY_SERVICE_API_KEY:?...}` (docker-compose.yml:154), so on that stack the service key is always set, the Auth Core provider always wins over `MODEL_PLANE_TOKEN`, and the documented dev path ends in case 3 whatever token an override file adds. It works only if the override also sets the key to an empty string (and `QUARRY_CROSS_PLANE_AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=1`). The deploy compose (`:-`) is fine. Add the empty-key override to the runbook, or prove the path once on a side-by-side stack.
