+# Rules for every build agent on branch mp-w2w3
+
+Worktree: `C:\dev\CoresSystem\.claude\worktrees\mp-w2w3-350537` (branch `mp-w2w3`). Other agents work in the SAME worktree at the same time on other crates, so:
+
+1. **Touch only the files of your lane** (named in your prompt). If you must touch a file outside it (e.g. a struct-literal compile fix after a proto change), keep the hunk minimal (`..Default::default()`), and list it in your report.
+2. **Your own Cargo target dir**: always `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=C:/dev/mp-w2w3-target-<lane>` and `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`. Run cargo from `apps/Model Plane/rust`. Never `cargo test --workspace` (two targets fail pre-existing on Windows: `inference-core` main.rs `tokio::signal::unix`, and `model-gateway/tests/e2e_invoke_chain_test.rs`). Use `cargo test -p <crate> --lib <filter>` (one filter per run) and named `--test <file>`. Long builds: run them in the foreground with a 600000 ms timeout, or in the background and wait for the notification.
+   If a test result contradicts the tree (an item that exists reported as unresolved), the target is stale: `cargo clean -p <crate>` in your target dir and retry.
+3. **Go**: `GOWORK=off go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` inside the service dir. No `-race` (no cgo). For Postgres integration tests use the scratch container already running: `TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:scratch@127.0.0.1:55439/postgres?sslmode=disable` (container `mpw2w3-pg`; create your own database inside it if the test needs one). Never touch any other container. Never start Docker Desktop. Never run `compose up`, never restart or swap a live container.
