+6. **Flags**: every new behaviour behind a flag that defaults OFF (env var, literal `1`/`true`/`on` to enable, anything else off). Pin the default-off in a test.
+7. **Secrets**: never read, print or grep `.env*` files or token values.
+8. **Commits**: commit your own work, local only, with explicit paths: `git add <paths> && git commit -m "<conventional msg>" -- <paths>` is NOT needed; use `git add <exact paths>` then `git commit -m ...`. If `index.lock` exists, wait 5 s and retry (another agent is committing). Never `--no-verify`, never amend, never reset/checkout/stash/clean/revert. Conventional Commits (`feat(execution-core): ...`), body explains why, and end the message with the line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Commit after each slice, not at the end.
+9. **Wave first**: build each slice to the plan scope with its named unit tests; one self-review pass at most. Anything deeper (a real gap, an unproven assumption, a plan statement that does not hold) goes as a bullet into `.plan-work/quarry-w1w2/mp-w2w3/DEPTH.md` (append, prefix with your lane and slice id). Do not loop on review fixes.
