+11. **Progress file**: `.plan-work/quarry-w1w2/mp-w2w3/progress-<lane>.md`: per slice: built (files), tests run (exact command + result counts), commits, flags, assumed decisions (defaults taken), not verified. Update it after each slice so a stop on a limit loses nothing. Commit it with the slice.
+13. **Shared files (lesson from batch 1)**: before editing a file outside your lane, run `git diff -- <file>`. If another lane already has uncommitted hunks there, do NOT add the same fix again (batch 1 ended with duplicated `..Default::default()` lines inside `json!` blocks and a non-compiling commit). Commit only the files you created or own. If a shared file must be committed, `cargo check` the affected crate first. `Envelope` (mp-events) now derives `Default`.
+12. **Final message** (to the lead, short): per slice built/tested/commit sha, plus anything blocking.
