+- [A / WS8.G] BLOCKER for live use, not in my files: `runtime_loop/browser_grant_approval.rs::satisfies_high_risk_ask` accepts only a grant of kind `run`. An attach grant (kind `attach`, parent = the person's run grant, owner = the user) therefore never satisfies the browser tool's high-risk `ask`, so a durable attached run would park on a durable approval (or be refused) at the outer gate. Proposed one-line change: accept `run | attach` there (both are user-bearer derived, both name a parent and the owner), plus a test. Listed under Lead to land.
