+- [A / E3.2-c] The redirect text is not scrubbed in the sink; it is covered by the planner-request boundary scrub (WS12.S4b) only. It is also not published on the timeline (the event still says `denied` with no reason), so the SPA must show the person's own text from its card.
+- [A / E3.3-f] There is no steer-without-pause RPC: the text rides PauseRun/ResumeRun. A client that wants to steer a running run without pausing it calls `resume` with text (queued, reported `running`). A dedicated `SteerRun` RPC would be cleaner; additive when wanted. No timeline event marks that a steer was delivered to the planner (no proto event exists), so the person cannot see when their text was read. The queue is in memory per execution-core process (like the pause state): lost on restart, not shared across replicas.
+- [A / E3.3-f] A steer queued while the loop waits inside an approval stays queued until the next step boundary after the decision; the approval wait itself never reads it (by design: it cannot approve).
+- [A / E3.3-l] Quarry has no truncation signal for its 50-target cap, so the planner view cannot say "N more targets exist"; the view's `omitted_targets` is therefore always 0 against today's Quarry. `warnings[]` and `settle_ms` do not exist on Quarry's observation yet; the lenient fields are inert until it adds them, and the shape of a warning (string vs object) is a guess covered by reading both.
+- [A / E3.3-l] Console text and request URLs are page-authored and enter the planner prompt inside the untrusted frame when the switch is on; they are screened by the same injection scanner as page text (added to the screening corpus) but no corpus run measured the effect.
+- [A / E3.2-e2] The tab actions are parsed but not advertised in `browser_tool_defs`' `browser.act` schema, so no model emits them; advertising them needs the exact-name tests and the tool catalogue golden updated (WS9.E files). An attached run's delegate cannot open/select/close (Quarry's owner-only rule); only list works there. `tab_new` with a URL is governed by Quarry's grant/web-policy check on top of the client-side domain check; `tab_new` without a URL opens a blank tab on a run with no URL constraint.
+- [A / E3.2-a] `host_class` is a coarse deterministic class (private/local host => `internal`, sign-in or payment step on a public host => `sensitive`, else `general`), not a real data-sensitivity classification of the site (no bank/health/gov list). It is computed from the gated action's URL (for a click that is the page URL the action carries), so a click on a page whose planner URL is empty reads `none`. The decision event's `decided_by` for a fail-closed gate is `system:fail-closed` (new label); the cancel and timeout labels are the ones already sent to DecideApproval.
