+# L-SC7-billing
+
+- Leg: L-SC7-billing. SC7 crawl clause (finite default page bound) and BILLING-IDEMPOTENCY (runbook section 4).
+- Time window UTC: 2026-10-28 17:12 to 17:15.
+- Image revision: `GET /version` returned `{"build_date":"2026-10-28T16:14:47Z","cargo_version":"0.1.0","revision":"qv2e-bd61260ee","service":"quarry-edge-rs"}`.
+- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer dev-evidence` (dev bypass, stub identity `org_placeholder` / `user_placeholder`).
+- Flags: none changed in this leg. `qv2e-flags.env` equals the copy taken at the start (`diff` empty). Nothing added to `flags-log.md`. The relevant baseline values: `QUARRY_EDGE__NATS_URL` set in the compose file, `QUARRY_EDGE__USAGE_BROWSER_METRICS` unset (edge log: `usage browser metrics mode` = `off`), so the legacy meter rule runs.
+- Usage meter: the edge publishes each event to NATS subject `usage.<metric>` through `NatsUsageMeter` (`crates/quarry-runtime/src/usage.rs`, `subject_for`). The event id is `quarry:<job_id>:<metric>`. The crawl event is metric `quarry.crawl.seed`, emitted in `crates/quarry-edge/src/routes.rs` after the handoff, keyed by `crate::handoff::billable_job_id(&ack)` (`crates/quarry-edge/src/handoff.rs`). The edge log at boot says `usage meter: NATS (publishes to usage.>)`.
+- How the events were observed: helper container `qv2e-helper-natssub` (image natsio/nats-box, network `qv2e-net`) ran `nats sub "usage.>"` as a plain subscriber. The NATS token was passed from the secrets file by environment variable inside one command and never printed. The qv2e NATS has only the stream `QUARRY_EVENTS` (subjects `quarry.>`) and no stream for `usage.>`, because billing-core creates that stream and it is not in this stack. A plain subscriber still receives the messages, so the observation is valid. Transcript: `L-SC7-billing-nats.log`. The helper was stopped (it removes itself, `--rm`); `docker ps -a` shows no `qv2e-helper-*` container.
+- Raw HTTP responses (no secrets): `L-SC7-billing-a.raw`, `-b.raw`, `-idem1.raw`, `-idem2.raw`, `-handofffail.raw`.
+
+## Results
+
+| id | what | result | evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| SC7.1 | `POST /v1/crawl` with no `max_pages` gets a finite default and says so | PASS | Seed `http://fixture-a.crawl.test/`. HTTP 200, job `job_01M61QZVY04YPRBQYXX58C6TVE`. `data.limits.max_pages` = `{"requested":null,"effective":1000,"clamped_by":["default"]}`; `data.limits.max_depth` = `{"requested":null,"effective":5,"clamped_by":["default"]}`; `data.effective.max_pages` 1000. This matches `docs/CONTRACTS.md` section 9.4. Job row in `quarry_v2.jobs`: `params.max_pages` 1000, `max_pages_requested` null. |
+| SC7.2 | `POST /v1/crawl` with `max_pages:0` gets the same finite default (zero is never unlimited, not a 400) | PASS | HTTP 200, job `job_01M61QZW2HX6NXYND4CSYCC6VB`. `limits.max_pages` = `{"requested":0,"effective":1000,"clamped_by":["default"]}`. Job row: `params.max_pages` 1000, `max_pages_requested` 0. |
+| SC7.3 | `constraints` and `clamped[]` in the response | NOT-RUN (not present) | Neither field exists in the `POST /v1/crawl` answer. The shape is `data.limits.{max_pages,max_depth}.{requested,effective,clamped_by}` plus `data.effective` (scope, robots, bounds, `request_warnings`, `warnings`). `effective.warnings` is `[]` for a default clamp. The status document of both jobs (`GET /v1/crawl/{id}`) has `total` 1000, `total_kind` `budget`, `warnings` `[]`. This is consistent with `CONTRACTS.md` (the `max_pages_clamped` warning is for a requested limit that was lowered, not for a default). See Depth 1. |
+| SC7.4 | both jobs finish | PASS | Both `completed` / `run_completed` in `quarry_v2.jobs` about 12 s after submit (`GET /v1/crawl/<id>`: `completed` 9, `failed` 1 for the first job). No cancel was needed. |
+| BI.1 | same crawl twice with the same `Idempotency-Key`: the second answer is a replay (control 200, same job id) | PASS | Key `sc7-billing-1793207602`, body `{"url":"http://fixture-a.crawl.test/","max_pages":3}`. Both edge answers HTTP 200 with the same `job_id` `job_01M61R13MKM61K79BBQVX4NVNH`. Control log (`qv2e-control`) for the two `POST /v1/jobs`: first `status=201` at 17:13:22Z, second `status=200` at 17:13:23Z. `quarry_v2.jobs` holds one row with that key. (The edge itself answers 200 for both, so the replay shows only in control's log and in the missing usage event.) |
+| BI.2 | one usage event keyed `quarry:<job_id>:<metric>` for the first submit, none for the replay | PASS | Subscriber on `usage.>`: exactly one event for the two submits, `event_id` `quarry:job_01M61R13MKM61K79BBQVX4NVNH:quarry.crawl.seed`, subject `usage.quarry.crawl.seed`, quantity 1.0, org `org_placeholder`, metadata `max_pages` 3. Counts: 2 events for the two SC7 crawls (distinct job ids, no key), 1 for the keyed pair, 1 more for a later control crawl after recovery (4 in all, all distinct job ids). The event id uses Control's job id, as `billable_job_id` requires. |
+| BI.3 | handoff fails (control stopped): no usage event | PASS | `docker stop qv2e-control` at 17:13:54Z. `POST /v1/crawl` without a key: HTTP 502, `UPSTREAM_BLOCKED`, "control unreachable: error sending request", `retryable:true`. The same with the idempotency header set to a fixed test value: HTTP 502, same body. Subscriber count stayed at 3 before and after both requests and after control was healthy again (checked again 40 s later). `quarry_v2.jobs` has 0 rows with key `sc7-handoff-fail-1`. |
+| BI.4 | control restarted, stack healthy, billing works again | PASS | `docker start qv2e-control`, healthy after about 10 s. `qv2e.sh ps`: all ten services healthy. `/ready` 200. A new crawl (`job_01M61R382EZRGNZCPNERXBZ46A`, `max_pages` 2) was accepted, completed, and gave event #4 `quarry:job_01M61R382EZRGNZCPNERXBZ46A:quarry.crawl.seed`. |
+| BI.5 | corrected-rules path (`QUARRY_EDGE__USAGE_BROWSER_METRICS=on`) behaves the same | NOT-RUN | Not asked for in this leg and no flag was changed. Both branches in `routes.rs` take the job id from the same `billable_job_id`, so the rule is the same by code reading; the wire test `handoff.rs` (status 200 with key = replay, no event) covers it. The stack run covers the default branch (`off`). |
+| FLAGS | every flag at baseline, edge healthy | PASS | `diff` of `qv2e-flags.env` against `l-sc7-flags-start.env` is empty. The edge was not restarted in this leg (up since 17:09:44Z); `/version` `qv2e-bd61260ee`; `/ready` 200. |
+
+## Depth
+
+1. **No `constraints` or `clamped[]` in the crawl answer.** The task text expected them "if present". They are not. The answer reports a clamp only through `limits.*.clamped_by` (`default` or `hard`). A default clamp is not repeated as a warning (`effective.warnings` is `[]`, the status document `warnings` is `[]`). A client that wants to know "my `max_pages:0` became 1000" must read `limits.max_pages.requested` and `clamped_by`. Not a FAIL.
+2. **A replay is invisible on the edge wire.** The first and second answer of the keyed pair are both HTTP 200 with the same body shape (only `accepted_at` differs). The replay shows only in Control (200 instead of 201) and in the missing usage event. `HandoffAck.replayed` is `#[serde(skip)]` on purpose (`routes.rs`, near line 1330). A client cannot tell a replay from a first submit. Not a FAIL; worth knowing for the SPA and the gateway.
+3. **The qv2e NATS has no `usage.>` stream.** With billing-core absent, `js.publish` gets no stream acknowledgement, so the publisher's task has nothing to confirm. A plain subscriber still saw every event. In the real stack billing-core owns the stream. This stack therefore proves what the edge publishes, not what billing-core stores or dedupes.
+4. **Control-down failure is clean.** The 502 returns in about 4 s (the edge waits for the connect error). No job row, no usage event, and the same status for a keyed and an unkeyed request.
+5. **First SC7 job counts `failed` 1.** Job `job_01M61QZVY04YPRBQYXX58C6TVE` finished with 9 pages completed and 1 failed (not looked into; outside this leg). The job state is `completed`, `run_completed`.
+
+## Not run
+
+- SC7.3 (`constraints`, `clamped[]`): the fields do not exist, see Depth 1.
+- BI.5 (usage mode `on`): not asked for, no flag changes in this leg.
+- Billing-core side (dedupe on `event_id`, Lago): no billing-core on qv2e.
