+- Time window UTC: 2026-10-28 19:56 to 20:02.
+- Code that runs: main + integration 7c082825a (live checkout `C:\dev\CoresSystem`). `GET /version` on the live edge returns `revision: "unverified"` (no build arg on live), so the revision is not proven by the endpoint.
+- Script: `apps/Ingestion Plane/Quarry-v2/scripts/e2e/crawl-scope-robots.sh`, run once per leg with `EDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082 CONTROL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:28081 FIXTURE_A_CONTAINER=crawl-fixture-a FIXTURE_B_CONTAINER=crawl-fixture-b DEV_BEARER=dev-evidence EVIDENCE_DIR=<this folder>/x10/<leg>`. The unreachable and redirect legs also had `UNREACHABLE_SEED_URL`, `FIXTURE_UNREACHABLE_CONTAINER`, `REDIRECT_SEED_URL`, `FIXTURE_REDIRECT_CONTAINER`. Per leg the script writes `fixture-a.log`, `fixture-b.log`, `job.json`, `crawl-response.json` under `x10/<leg>/`. I added `run-events.json` (the run events read from `GET /v1/runs/<run_id>/events`) for the enforce, unreachable and redirect legs. Leg logs: `L-X10-robots-<leg>.log`. Metric snapshots: `x10/<leg>-metrics.txt`.
+- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer dev-evidence` (dev bypass: stub org_placeholder / user_placeholder, principal user). The D2-161 check calls `/v1/internal/run_page` the way the orchestrator does. The runtime token and the internal secret were read from the edge container's own environment inside one shell command and never printed.
+- Edge flags per leg, set in `live-flags.env`, applied with `live.sh edge-up` and checked against the running container BEFORE each leg (the helper compares the file to `docker exec quarry-edge printenv` and stops on a mismatch; no restart failed this time): legacy `CRAWL_ROBOTS=off` with `CRAWL_SCOPE_MODE` unset (code default observe); observe `CRAWL_ROBOTS=observe` and `CRAWL_SCOPE_MODE=observe`; enforce `CRAWL_ROBOTS=enforce` and `CRAWL_SCOPE_MODE=enforce`. `ROBOTS_UNREACHABLE=disallow` (baseline) all the time. I also set `QUARRY_EDGE__METRICS_ENABLED=1` for the whole leg so the counters can be read (the baseline has it at 0). Every change is in `flags-log.md`.
+- Fixture logs: `crawl-fixture-a` and `crawl-fixture-b` were restarted before the legacy, observe and enforce legs and before the D2-161 check. The script also reads only log lines since its own start.
+- Metric shape: `docker exec quarry-edge sh -c 'wget -q -O - --header="Authorization: Bearer $QUARRY_EDGE__METRICS_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:9092/metrics'`, filtered for `quarry_robots` and `quarry_cache`. An edge restart resets the counters, so each leg starts at 0, except the unreachable and redirect legs, which ran on the same edge process as the enforce leg (counters carry on).
