+# P0-live
+
+- Leg: P0-live (runbook section 1 steps 1 and 5, section 4 list A rows that need no user), on the live dev stack.
+- Time window UTC: 2026-10-28 19:49 to 19:55.
+- Code that runs: main + integration 7c082825a. `/version` says revision "unverified" (live has no build arg).
+- Auth for the dev calls: the literal `Bearer dev-evidence` (stub org_placeholder).
+- Flag change: one. `QUARRY_EDGE__METRICS_ENABLED` 0 -> 1 at 19:50:14 so the internal metrics listener runs (it is off by default on live), reverted at 19:54:03. `live-flags.env` is empty again, the edge was recreated, `live.sh flags` shows the 22 baseline values (copy: `P0-live-flags-end.txt`), the edge is healthy. Both lines are in `flags-log.md`.
+- Transcripts next to this file: `P0-live-metrics-start.log`, `P0-live-metrics-end.log`, `P0-live-edge.log` (edge log of the metrics-on window, boot to 19:53), `P0-live-flags-end.txt`.
+
+## Results
+
+| id | what | result | evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| a | services running and healthy | PASS | `docker ps`: quarry-edge, quarry-control, quarry-orchestrator all `(healthy)`. crawl-fixture-a and crawl-fixture-b are `Up` (nginx has no healthcheck). Also healthy: verevon-gateway-rs, the SPA container, ingestion-postgres, ingestion-nats. |
+| b | edge `/health`, `/ready`, `/version` | PASS | `/health` 200 `ok`. `/ready` 200 `status: ready`, `durable: true`, both browser pools `state: idle`, slot 0 `starting`, 0 sessions, max_sessions 40. `/version` 200 `{"revision":"unverified","service":"quarry-edge-rs","cargo_version":"0.1.0"}`. |
+| c | flags against README baseline and runbook defaults | PASS | `live.sh flags` at 19:49, and again at 19:54 after the revert: the same 22 lines. All equal the README baseline (no difference). Against the runbook section 1 step 5: SCRAPE_ACTIONS off, SCRAPE_CAPTURE off, CRAWL_ROBOTS observe, ROBOTS_UNREACHABLE disallow, BUDGET_ENFORCEMENT shadow, AUTOPROMPT 0, SEMANTIC_RERANK 0, LLM_CLASSIFY_INTENT 0, PAGE_TITLE_ENRICH 0, MODEL_PLANE_URL empty: all match. Differences from a production-like stack, all expected for live dev: ENVIRONMENT=dev, AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=1, ARTIFACT_BACKEND=memory, RUN_SWEEPER_DRY_RUN=1, PROFILE_ENCRYPTION=off, ANSWER_SYNTHESIS, AI_FORMATS, MODEL_AUDIO, SEARCH_SUGGEST, ZERO_SAAS_SEARCH all 0. Not set (code default): PROFILE_OWNER_ENFORCE, TAKEOVER_ENFORCEMENT, RECEIPT_TEXT_MODE, CRAWL_SCOPE_MODE, AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_STEPS, DOC_ROUTING, VECTOR_RETRIEVAL. Other values seen in the edge env: SEMANTIC_RERANK_TOP_N=10, RERANK_DEADLINE_MS=2000, RERANK_SHADOW=1, QUARRY_SCRAPE_HEAVY_PERMITS=1. |
+| d0 | metrics listener on live | PARTIAL | Default on live is `QUARRY_EDGE__METRICS_ENABLED=0` (compose `docker-compose.yml:278`), no token set, so nothing listens on :9092 and the runbook command (with `$QUARRY_EDGE__METRICS_TOKEN`) fails with "connection refused" and an empty token. I turned the listener on for this leg (see header) and read it without a token: `docker exec quarry-edge sh -c 'wget -q -O - http://127.0.0.1:9092/metrics'`. In dev there is no token requirement (`metrics.rs:100`: only production needs one). PARTIAL because the baseline edge cannot be scraped. |
+| d1 | `quarry_robots_decisions_total` | PASS | Present, 5 series, all 0 at the start and at the end: mode=enforce outcome=denied and unreachable, mode=observe would_deny and would_unreachable, mode=any allowed. |
+| d2 | `quarry_agent_budget_exhausted_total` | PASS (absent) | 0 series at the start and at the end. The family is created at the first event (defined in `metrics.rs`). No agent run happened, so absent is the expected value. |
+| d3 | `quarry_agent_takeover_exempt_steps_total` | PASS (absent) | 0 series, same reason. |
+| d4 | `quarry_profile_owner_decisions_total` | PASS (absent) | 0 series. No run with a persistent profile was started (that needs a browser run, out of this leg). |
+| d5 | `quarry_profile_owner_stamps_total` | PASS (absent) | 0 series, same reason. |
