+# R-SC4 (re-run of SC4 T1-T3 on live dev, after the SC4 fixes)
+
+- Leg: R-SC4, re-run of L-SC3-SC4-runs rows T1, T2, T3 (and its Depth 1-2), plus T4 (held subresource) and T5 (slot and log checks).
+- Time window UTC: 2026-10-28 23:12:07 to 23:23:30 (2026-10-29 CET).
+- Code that runs: quarry-edge rebuilt from the live checkout `C:/dev/CoresSystem` with the fix commits 041a7cd2b + 33bf15174 (SC4) and the others named in the task. The live `quarry-browser/src/chromiumoxide.rs` equals the worktree's file except for line endings (same line numbers). Shipped deadlines read from the live tree: navigate 25 000 ms, ax_snapshot 10 000 ms, navigate_recovery 3 000 ms (`quarry-browser/src/deadlines.rs:205`, `:207`, `:228`).
+- Identity: the dev stub (`Bearer dev-evidence`), every run started with `initiated_by:"agent"` and `allowed_domains [fixture-a.crawl.test, slow.crawl.test]`.
+- Helper: `qlive-rerun-slow` (nginx:alpine, alias slow.crawl.test on network crawl-fixture). `/slow.html`: `limit_rate 1` on a 300 KB body (the load never ends, the document never commits within the deadline). `/held.html`: a small page served at full speed whose `<img src="/held/pixel.png">` is under `limit_rate 1` (the HTML arrives, the load event never fires). Recipe: R-SC4-helper.sh.txt. Removed at the end (`docker ps -a --filter name=qlive-rerun-slow` empty).
+- Flags: one change, `QUARRY_BROWSER_DEADLINE_SCALE` (unset) -> 0.5 for T2 (the same non-`QUARRY_EDGE__` name the original leg used), reverted. Logged in flags-log.md under "## Re-run 2026-10-29". At the end live-flags.env is empty, the edge was recreated (healthy), `live.sh flags | diff - P0-live-flags-end.txt` is empty (R-SC4-flags-end.txt). `/ready` at the end: status ready, sessions_open 0.
+- Every run started was closed (DELETE 200, 19 runs). `/ready` sessions_open was 0 before each edge recreate.
+
+## Checks
+
+| id | check | result | evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| T1 | Typed TIMEOUT at the SHIPPED navigate deadline (no scale override): navigate to `http://slow.crawl.test/slow.html` | PASS | 8 of 8 hangs (6 in R-SC4-t1-t3-shipped.log, 2 on the final container in R-SC4-t5-final-container.log): HTTP 504 after 25.019 to 25.063 s (was 502 at 30.01 s), body `error.code=TIMEOUT`, message "browser operation navigate timed out", `retryable:false`, `details={deadline_ms:25000, effect:"unknown", op:"navigate"}`. No URL in any body: `grep -c 'http://'` 0 and `slow.crawl.test` 0 in each hang body (20 of 20 TIMEOUT bodies of the leg). Raw body: R-SC4-t1-hang-body.raw. Receipts mark the step `failed`. |
+| T3a | After each T1 TIMEOUT, the next step on the same run is a navigate to `http://fixture-a.crawl.test/` | PASS | 4 of 4 (3 + 1 on the final container): 200 in 0.200 to 0.351 s, title "Fixture A", 37 AX nodes, no `ax_snapshot` in the body. The step after it (wait) 200 in 0.16 to 0.21 s. Was: 504 after 15.8 to 16.2 s. |
+| T3b | After each T1 TIMEOUT, the next step in another run is a wait step | PASS | 4 of 4 (3 + 1): 200 in 0.164 to 0.224 s, observation url `http://fixture-a.crawl.test/`, title "Fixture A" (the hang never committed, so the previous page is kept), 37 AX nodes, 0 `ax_snapshot` TIMEOUT. Was: 504 `ax_snapshot` after 20.1 to 21.4 s. |
+| T2 | Same with `QUARRY_BROWSER_DEADLINE_SCALE=0.5` | PASS | 6 of 6 hangs (4 in R-SC4-t2-scale05.log, 2 back to back in R-SC4-extra-scale05.log E1): 504 after 12.528 to 12.602 s, `TIMEOUT`, `details={deadline_ms:12500, effect:"unknown", op:"navigate"}`, no URL in the body (R-SC4-t2-hang-body.raw). Next step: navigate 200 in 0.23 and 0.33 s, wait 200 in 0.16 and 0.16 s; after two hangs in a row the next navigate 200 in 0.25 s (E1). |
+| T4 | Page whose HTML loads but an `<img>` never finishes (`/held.html`), after a prior page in the run | PASS | 3 of 3 (2 in R-SC4-t4-held.log, 1 in R-SC4-t5-final-container.log): navigate 504 `TIMEOUT` after 25.013 to 25.052 s, `deadline_ms:25000`, no URL in the body. Next wait step 200 in 0.15 to 0.20 s with url `http://slow.crawl.test/held.html`, title "R-SC4 held image page", 10 AX nodes including "Held image" and "The image below never finishes." (not about:blank). `browser-session` currentUrl is the held page. The navigate after it: 200 "Fixture A" in 0.18 to 0.28 s. |
+| T4b | The same held page (and the never-committing slow page) as the FIRST step of a run (no page before it) | FAIL | 3 of 3: navigate 504 `TIMEOUT` as expected (held page 25.12 s twice; slow page at scale 0.5 12.60 s, E2), but the next wait step answers HTTP 502 `DRIVER_FAILED` "chromiumoxide: no current page; call goto() first", `details={reason:"no_current_page"}`, `retryable:false` in 0.11 to 0.12 s; `browser-session` currentUrl "". The held page's title is never observable. A navigate after it works (200 "Fixture A"). Body: R-SC4-first-step-wait-body.raw. See Depth 1. Not in the original leg's rows; found by this leg. |
+| T5a | `/ready` slot generation unchanged through the leg | PASS | Three edge containers (two planned recreates for the flag change and its revert). In each: generation 0 until the first run, then 1, and still 1 after every run and at the end of each phase (logged after every close in each .log). No relaunch beyond the planned recreates. |
+| T5b | No browser relaunch or crash lines in `docker logs quarry-edge` | PASS | R-SC4-edge-scan.log: 0 lines matching relaunch, crash, lost, disconnect, dead, recycled, unhealthy in the scale-0.5 container (143 lines, since 23:12:07Z) and in the final container (67 lines, since 23:21:05Z). The first container's log (T1/T4 23:12-23:17Z) is gone with the recreate; T1, T3a, T3b and T4 were repeated on the final container for this scan. |
+| T5c | The slow URL host in the edge log | PASS | 0 lines with `slow.crawl.test`, `slow.html` or `held.html` in either log. The error lines are tower_http `response failed` with status and latency only (504 at 12.5 s x7 and 25.0 to 25.1 s x4; 502 at 109 to 111 ms x2 = the T4b waits). The error bodies carry no URL (T1). |
+
+## Compared with the original leg
+
+- T1: FAIL (502 DRIVER_FAILED at 30.01 s, `details.url`) -> PASS (504 TIMEOUT at 25.02 to 25.06 s, no URL). Depth 1 of the original leg is fixed.
+- T3: FAIL (next step 504 after 15 to 21 s) -> PASS (next step 200 in 0.16 to 0.35 s, at both scales, also after two hangs in a row). Depth 2 of the original leg is fixed for a run that already has a page.
+- T2: PASS -> PASS (the deadline is now 12.5 s at scale 0.5 because navigate is 25 s).
+
+## Depth
+
+1. **A navigate TIMEOUT on a run's first step closes the tab, so the next step is a non-retryable 502 (T4b).** In `goto`, the recovery that keeps the page after a TIMEOUT runs only when the tab already exists (`quarry-browser/src/chromiumoxide.rs:3920`, `if !created`). A run with no tab goes through `open_tab_page`, whose first navigation has no recovery by design (`chromiumoxide.rs:1597-1600`, "a tab whose first navigation fails is closed by the attach guard"). The next observation then finds no page and answers `DRIVER_FAILED` `no_current_page`, `retryable:false` (`chromiumoxide.rs:1262-1270`). Effects: (a) a page whose HTML arrived but whose load never ended (held image, long-poll, analytics beacon) is readable when it is the second navigation of a run but not when it is the first; (b) an agent that gets a TIMEOUT on step 0 and then observes gets a 502 that says "not retryable", although a navigate on the same run works (200). Options for the lead: commit the tab in `open_tab_page` on a navigate TIMEOUT the same way `goto` does (stop the load, mark the tab abandoned, keep it), or answer the no-page case after a first-step TIMEOUT with a typed, retryable error. Not fixed here.
+2. The T3 result depends on the hang not committing: for `/slow.html` the observation after the TIMEOUT shows the previous page (fixture-a), not about:blank and not the slow URL. That matches the 33bf15174 design ("the page, old or new, is readable at once").
+3. chromiumoxide logs `WS Invalid message: data did not match any variant of untagged enum Message` (WARN) a few times per run (7 in the final container). Seen in earlier legs too; unrelated to the timeout, noise only.
+4. `/ready` generation resets to 0 at every edge recreate and becomes 1 at the first run; a relaunch check across a flag change has to compare per container, as done here.
+
+## Not run
+
+- `pdf` at its new 25 s deadline (the commit also lowered it): no row asked for it.
+- A WebSocket frames viewer during the hang.
