+A deployed stack cannot turn this on yet. The Quarry to Model Plane grant for the chat lane (decision X-7: two audiences, `model-gateway` and `inference-core`, retention `tenant`, and the two manifest rows set `granted: true`) and the metered service lane on the gateway (WS16.S1) are owner decisions that are not made; until then Quarry holds no credential for this lane outside the dev bypass. A user token may ask; a service principal needs the scope `extract:ai` (no registry principal holds it); a request labelled `initiated_by: "agent"` is refused. The contract is `docs/CONTRACTS.md`, "Scrape AI formats"; the operator steps are in `docs/RUNBOOKS.md`.
+
+**Structured extract (`POST /v1/extract` with `schema` or `prompt`; INNH-2, INNH-3).** It has no switch of its own, but it is one of the QB-T17 Model Plane features (the table below) and `QUARRY_EDGE__AI_FORMATS` gates it: with the switch off, or refused at boot because no model path exists, a schema or prompt request answers 501 `UNSUPPORTED` ("structured extraction is not available on this edge: QUARRY_EDGE__AI_FORMATS is off") when a Model Plane URL is set. It calls the gateway's `POST /v1/invoke` and needs `QUARRY_EDGE__MODEL_PLANE_URL` and a model credential: the Auth Core minted token (`QUARRY_EDGE__QUARRY_SERVICE_API_KEY`; the `model-invoke` row is not granted) or, under the cross-plane auth dev bypass, `QUARRY_EDGE__MODEL_PLANE_TOKEN`. Without them the answer is a 501 `UNSUPPORTED` that says which is missing (three texts, `docs/ERROR_REASONS.md`); a deployed stack always gets one until WS16.S1 to S3 and decision X-7 land. Setting the URL alone is not enough. The operator steps and what works in development are in `docs/RUNBOOKS.md`, "Enable structured extract and AI formats".
+
+**Answer synthesis (`/v1/answer`, `/v1/answer/stream`, `include_answer`; INNH-8a).** One pipeline (search, read the top pages, ask the Model Plane) serves the three surfaces. It is off: `QUARRY_EDGE__ANSWER_SYNTHESIS` must be `1`, `true` or `on` (compose variable `QUARRY_EDGE_ANSWER_SYNTHESIS`, default `0`), and `MODEL_PLANE_URL` alone does not turn it on. It is one of the QB-T17 switches (the table below), so the boot gate also needs a model path for it: a granted `model-invoke` manifest row, or the development bypass credential. A deployed stack has neither (the cross-plane grant is owner decision INNH-8b), so a switch that is on there is refused at boot and `/v1/answer` answers 501 `model_path_refused`. It also needs a search provider and `QUARRY_EDGE__MODEL_PLANE_URL`. When a gate is closed the answer says which, in `reason` (`/v1/answer`: 501 `synthesis_disabled`, `model_path_refused`, `no_search_provider`, `no_model_plane_url` or `model_client_init_failed`; 503 `model_plane_auth_refused` when a wired call is refused) and in `answer_status` / `answer_reason` on `POST /v1/search`. A zero data retention request is refused with a 403 `zdr_unavailable` before any work. Operator steps: `docs/RUNBOOKS.md`, "Answer synthesis".
